<CapyPlopInfo title="Small springs. Tricky jumps." description="Capy Plop is a native capybara hopping game for iPhone and iPad. Hold, hop and aim for a perfect plop.">
  <p><strong>Hold. Hop. Plop.</strong> Guide a calm capybara between tiny hot springs. Hold to charge a jump, release to hop, and aim for the middle. Smaller pools, drifting springs and playful water hazards make the next landing a little trickier.</p>
  <p>Play endless runs, explore sequential trails and collect up to three stars on each trail. Scores, stars and settings save on your device. There is no gameplay account.</p>
  <h2>A little more to explore</h2>
  <p>The first ten Cedar trails and unlimited endless attempts are included. The optional one-time Hot Springs Pass adds twenty trails in Blossom and Moonlight worlds, daily and weekly challenges, practice mode, four cosmetic outfits and one ad-free continue per run. No subscription. The shop shows Apple's current localized price before a purchase.</p>
  <p>Without the Pass, you can choose to watch a short, clearly labeled promotion for another app by Randy Torres for one continue. Skip is always available. You never have to click, download or buy the advertised app. Fresh attempts remain unlimited.</p>
  <h2>The orange stays put</h2>
  <p>The orange, leaf, towel, blossom, duck and crown are outfits. They change the capybara's look without changing its jumping or scoring. Earn the leaf with 25 lifetime plops, or choose one of the extra outfits included in the Pass.</p>
  <p>Capy Plop is made by Randy Torres under the RandyVentures name for iPhone and iPad, with adaptive layouts. Visit <a href="/capy-plop/support/">support</a> for controls, purchases and local progress, or read the <a href="/capy-plop/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</CapyPlopInfo>
